Non-vacuity check (AC-26): a third route with a route parameter
("/probe/{id}") was temporarily mapped and the suite re-run.
TheHostMapsExactlyTwoGetEndpoints and NoMappedEndpointTakesARouteParameter both
failed as intended. The route was removed and the full suite re-run green. This
is the assertion that drove the minimal-APIs-over-Razor-Pages decision in
architecture.md, so it had to be shown to bite.

Kestrel smoke test (beyond the in-process suite):
  GET /        -> 200, text/html; charset=utf-8, 252 bytes
  GET /health  -> 200, text/plain; charset=utf-8, 7 bytes
  No Server header emitted — this validates AddServerHeader = false over the
  wire, which TestServer structurally cannot check because it does not use
  Kestrel. Until now that setting was only asserted in source.

Resolved from T02:
  The Windows Application Control policy that blocked TaxCases.Tests during T02
  (0x800711C7) is no longer in effect. The project executes normally and its 337
  tests pass. The block was transient and environmental; nothing in the
  repository was changed to clear it. T02's marker records those 337 as inferred
  rather than verified — they are now verified.

  The underlying hazard T02 flagged still stands and is NOT fixed by this task:
  `dotnet test TaxAI.sln` returns exit code 0 when an assembly is skipped, so a
  green exit code is not proof that every test ran. Worth addressing separately.

